<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Blaj</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Blaj is a small town in Alba County, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romania">Romania</a>, in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/transylvania">Transylvania</a>. It became the seat of the Romanian Greek Catholic Church after the union of many <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eastern-orthodox-church">Orthodox</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romanians">Romanians</a> with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> around 1700, and its schools, opened in 1754, made it a cradle of the Romanian national movement. In May 1848 a great assembly of Romanians on its Field of Liberty demanded national rights.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/blaj.jpg" alt="Blaj" width="320" height="172" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Țetcu Mircea Rareș · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:RO_Blaj_2023_(30).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
